   "price_text": "Free",
   "is_free": true,
   "description": "The Hardware Behind the AI Buildout Hosted by ReuseTechBC and Vancouver Tech Journal AI ambitions are running into a physical reality. Every model deployment and copilot rollout raises a hardware question: what to buy, keep, or retire, and what it really costs. For the first time in years, hardware strategy is back on the CIO’s agenda. We’ll cover: Refresh cycles: Do AI workloads justify faster refreshes, or are we retiring hardware too early? The real cost of AI capacity: On-prem, cloud, or hybrid, and where the hidden costs are. Managing fleets at scale: Tracking and planning across thousands of devices as needs shift. The lifecycle question: How reuse, redeployment, and responsible disposition protect budgets and sustainability goals. Procurement meets sustainability: What a circular approach to IT looks like in practice. The discussion will be followed by dinner, drinks and networking! Who should attend: CIOs, IT and infrastructure leaders, IT asset managers, and procurement and sustainability teams. If you budget for, manage, or retire your organization’s hardware, this conversation is for you. SPEAKERS Sandeep Sidhu: Chief Information Officer, Emily Carr University Amrit Brar: Director, Technology Business Management Office, TransLink Christopher Chong: Founder, Skeena Data Centers Corporation Mary-Em Waddington: Executive Director, BC Technology for Learning Society / ReuseTechBC",
