   "id": "daf84701335a",
   "title": "White-Hat Security Community - Monthly Coffee Chat (#21) - 🏭 Cyber Meets Physical - Lessons from Europe's Freezer Hacks",
   "start": "2026-11-14T12:00-07:00",
   "end": "2026-11-14T14:00-07:00",
   "venue": "Deville Coffee - The Post, 366 Dunsmuir St, Vancouver, BC V6B 0T5, Canada",
   "city": "Vancouver, BC",
   "price_text": "Free",
   "is_free": true,
   "description": "Join us for a coffee chat hosted by the White-Hat Security Community. The anchoring topic for this month's event is: 🏭 Cyber Meets Physical - Lessons from Europe's Freezer Hacks ❄️ In October, attackers remotely switched the refrigeration controllers at hundreds of French supermarkets into defrost mode. At the start of November it happened again across Belgium, Ireland, Sweden and several other European countries, with some freezers reportedly hitting 50°C and stores throwing out stock. No malware, no ransom note, and no sophisticated exploit: just internet-exposed controllers and weak or default passwords. It's a good excuse to talk about operational technology (OT), the systems that run the physical world, and why securing a freezer is so different from securing a laptop. No industrial background required. Some of the areas we'll be discussing: Hackers defrosted freezers at 700 French supermarkets. Could the same thing happen here? Default passwords on internet-facing controllers in 2026: whose job was it to change them? No malware and no ransom note: what were the attackers actually trying to achieve? What's the strangest thing you've ever found connected to the internet at work? 🏭 Want to go deeper on OT and ICS security after this? Check out DMZ604, Parisa Saqib's new Vancouver community for infrastructure and industrial security: https://luma.com/calendar/cal-nmALoHASvmHmUaO This is an informal and welcoming coffee chat where cyber security professionals from all backgrounds can connect, share experiences, and build lasting relationships in a relaxed atmosphere. Whether you're just starting your journey in cyber security, transitioning from another field, or you're a seasoned expert, this event is designed for anyone passionate about the world of digital security. ☁️🔒 Grab your favorite drink - whether it’s coffee, tea, matcha, or juice - and dive into meaningful conversations about industry trends, career insights, personal stories, and the challenges and opportunities shaping the cyber security landscape. This is a safe, supportive space for learning, sharing, and connecting, no matter your experience, background, or role. Our goal is to foster a diverse, inclusive community where everyone feels valued, heard, and supported. Whether you’re seeking advice on breaking into the industry, eager to share best practices, or simply looking to connect with like-minded individuals, this is the perfect place for you. Come for the conversation, stay for the connections! ☕🔐 Who should attend: Cyber security and data privacy enthusiasts and professionals of all experience levels 👩‍💻👨‍💻 Those interested in expanding their network or learning from others 🌱💬 Anyone passionate about making the digital world safer! 🛡️ Professionals and enthusiasts in related areas including but not limited to secure software development, risk management, data governance, compliance, networking, intelligence, security software/hardware engineering, business continuity, cyber and privacy law, fraud prevention, or cyber insurance. 🔍 Who should not attend: Anyone intending to aggressively pitch themselves for jobs or promote products/services 🚫 Individuals who are not respectful of their peers 👎 Black hat hackers, of course! 👾 We look forward to seeing you there! 👀 For those that are new to the cyber security space or to the geographic area, I would also like to highlight a few other excellent cyber security communities that have been serving the Metro Vancouver region for years (to name some of my favorites): ISACA Vancouver Chapter (https://lu.ma/ISACA) VanCitySec (https://luma.com/vancitysec) DC604 (https://luma.com/dc604) OWASP Vancouver Chapter (https://www.eventbrite.com/o/120870731626) Women in CyberSecurity (WiCyS) Western Canada Affiliate (https://www.linkedin.com/company/wicys-western-canada-affiliate/) ISC2 Vancouver Chapter (https://infosecbc.org/category/events/) White Hat Cyber Crew (BCIT Student Club) (https://discord.com/invite/p4kFWtGUrD) Cyber Warriors (NYIT Student Club) (https://www.instagram.com/nyit_cyberwarriors/)",
