   "description": "What began at #HACKVAN2026 is now coming to life. Join us for Steward & Celebrate: an evening to witness the stewardship and celebration of redemptive tech builds. Live Project Demos Include: Planter Flow - An app that helps BC church planters plan, set, and share their goals so that they can be better supported and cared for. CareRide Platform - A platform for Salvation Army staff to request and coordinate free/paid transportation with partner organizations so that vulnerable clients can safely reach essential services. Event Details: 📅 Date: Tuesday, November 24th, 2026 ⏰ Time: 6:00 - 8:00 PM PCT 📍 Venue: 535 Smithe St, Vancouver Get a glimpse of tech shaped by faith where innovation serves the least of these. We’d be honoured to have you witness what God is doing through this community. =============================================== This event is for everyone from developers to ministry leaders to designers. Our goal is to join together with the broader community, using tech and innovation as a means to grow the Kingdom of God. What is FaithTech We are a global movement of Christians interested in all things faith and technology. Our goal is to provide an authentic community that learns and builds together at the intersection of faith and technology. You can learn from one of our experienced speakers, build projects that impact your world, and innovate with like-minded individuals. Visit our website at https://www.faithtech.com/ for more! * Photographs and videos may be taken during this event. Please contact us in advance if you would not like to be a part of videos and photos. Otherwise, by attending, you are agreeing to participate in our media. FaithTech in 44 seconds",
