   "id": "cf3ae29ddd2a",
   "title": "Your WAF Can’t Read: Prompt Injection and the Limits of Pattern-Matching Security",
   "start": "2026-12-04T14:00-07:00",
   "end": "2026-12-04T16:30-07:00",
   "venue": "555 W Hastings St #2360, Vancouver, BC, Canada",
   "city": "Vancouver, BC",
   "price_text": "Free",
   "is_free": true,
   "description": "Attention to all DevOps, Security, FinTech, and GenAI enthusiasts! Planview Vancouver Platform Engineering Team (FlowPlatform Team) is hosting a meetup at their office, bringing together techies across the city for a deep dive into securing AI agents on December 4th from 2:00 - 4:30 PM! Your WAF can block SQL injection in its sleep, but it can't read a prompt. A prompt injection is perfectly normal natural language, so there is no signature to match. Now that AI agents call APIs, run tools, and act with valid credentials, the traffic looks legitimate even when the agent has been tricked into doing the attack. This session explores why traditional security tooling struggles with agentic systems, what your WAF and delivery layer can and can't see, and how to build a layered defence with gateways, guardrails, least-privilege access, and human approval where it matters. Speakers: Tallal Mohar, Software Engineer Intern, Planview Scott McAllister, Community Evangelist, F5 & (Developer Advocate & Educator) Adetokunbo Ige, Senior Software Engineer (Platform Engineer), Planview & (CNCF Ambassador, AWS Community Builder, Ambassador Community Advocate - Ambassador Labs) Agenda: 2:00 - 2:30: Networking 2.30 - 3.00: AWS Agent Core Introduction to AWS Agent Core Agent Core Isolation Observability (AWS CloudTrail) AgentCore Harness 3:00 - 4:00: Your WAF Can't Read: Securing Agentic Systems Why signature-based security misses prompt injection When valid traffic does the damage: the confused deputy problem Layered defence: WAF, gateway, guardrails, and least privilege Open Discussion 4:00 - 4:30 — Closeout & Networking When and Where 📅 Date: Friday, December 4th, 2026 🕒 Time: 2:00 PM - 4:30 PM 📍 Location: Planview Vancouver office; 2360-555 Hastings St W Vancouver, BC V6B 4N6, Canada. You can take the elevator up to the 23rd floor, ring the doorbell for unit 2360 (Planview) Who should join? Any DevOps engineer, SRE, security engineer or AI enthusiast looking to understand how agentic AI changes the threat model, and what to put in front of it. Our Sponsors: Planview https://www.planview.com/ Agreements By registering for this event, you acknowledge and agree to the following: Photography: Photos taken during the event.",
