   "description": "Are you a tech professional seeking new opportunities? Join us for the Vancouver Tech Community: Connect with Tech Companies event, where local tech companies actively recruiting new talent will present their organizations and available positions. This exclusive networking event brings together hiring managers, recruiters, and founders from Vancouver's vibrant tech ecosystem who are currently looking to fill positions on their teams. Unlike traditional job fairs, this event offers a more intimate and conversational atmosphere where meaningful connections can be made. Event Highlights Company Spotlights: Selected companies will present brief overviews of their mission, products, workplace culture, and current openings Networking Sessions: Connect directly with hiring decision-makers in a relaxed environment Q&A Opportunities: Get your questions answered about potential employers, team dynamics, and specific roles Refreshments & Appetizers: Enjoy complimentary refreshments while networking with industry professionals Who Should Attend This event is perfect for software developers, data scientists, UX/UI designers, product managers, DevOps, Business Analyst, Sales, Marketing, Customer Success, and other tech professionals who are: Actively seeking new career opportunities Interested in learning about Vancouver's growing tech companies Looking to expand their professional network within the local tech community With only 50 spots available, this exclusive event is set to sell out fast. Don't miss this chance to showcase your skills and potentially find your next career opportunity with innovative Vancouver tech companies! 🔥 Book Your Ticket Now! About Careerin Tech Society: Careerin Tech Society, a nonprofit organization whose mission is to inspire, develop, and support innovators, entrepreneurs, and tech talents. We aim to connect people in the tech sector and build up the tech ecosystem in the Greater Vancouver area. Our events include Techstars Startup Weekend Vancouver, Vancouver Founders Huddle, and Vancouver Tech Community, among others. If you are interested in sponsoring, volunteering, please email kenneth.ip@careerin.org Subscribe to our event calendar to get updates when we have new events or programs available. https://lu.ma/careerintechevents Sponsor: Cartage - Meet Wilson. Your last logistics hire. Built for manufacturers and distributors. https://www.cartage.ai/ Venue Partner: Convergence and its sister companies Pixel Ramen (our UX Research & Design studio) and Giant Leap (our Machine Learning as a Service [MLaaS] platform) create award-winning digital products for businesses and public sector organizations, applying the latest trends in UX, web application development, AI/ML engineering and cloud computing to create world-class user experiences.",
