   "id": "a9b65a84216c",
   "title": "AI Happy Hour at FriendsQuarters #8: What Actually Shipped",
   "start": "2026-12-18T16:00-07:00",
   "end": "2026-12-18T19:00-07:00",
   "venue": "FriendsQuarters, 116 W Hastings St Unit 200, Vancouver, BC V6B 1G8, Canada",
   "city": "Vancouver, BC",
   "price_text": "$10 cad",
   "is_free": false,
   "description": "AHH FQ: AI Happy Hour at FriendsQuarters, December Edition. AHH FQ is a monthly, 3rd-Friday drop-in at FriendsQuarters for the BC + AI community. Come by after work, grab the drink that comes with your ticket, and talk to the people making this city more interesting. Yes, the initials are doing what you think they are doing. Then we get back to the room. No panel. No pitch circle. Just a room for chats, hangouts, and drinks, closing out the year. What This Is This is not a lecture night. It is not a demo day. It is not a room full of people pretending they came for the name tags. It is a monthly Friday happy hour: drop in, see the regulars, say hi to the new people, stand at the bar, compare notes, or ask the question you have been carrying around for a while. Stay a bit or stay the whole time. BC + AI already has the talks, labs, office hours, courses, and meetups that the city has embraced. AHH FQ is the loose space between all that. The place where the hallway conversation gets its own night. Why FriendsQuarters Dean and the FriendsQuarters crew invited this community into their space because FQ is already part co-working room, part media shop, part event floor, and part neighborhood hangout. FQ 116 has the right bones for this: brick, hardwood, atrium light, a bar, a media setup, and enough Gastown weirdness around the edges to keep it honest. It feels like a Vancouver room, not a hotel ballroom. Who It's For BC + AI regulars. FQ members. Builders, artists, researchers, founders, operators, designers, policy people, funders, teachers, students, skeptics, and the friend who keeps asking what this stuff is doing to work, art, power, and daily life. You don't need a pitch, a deck, or to be working on a startup. Bring a real question, a generous ear, or someone who should meet the room. How It Works Arrive anytime between 4:00 and 7:00 PM. Your $10 CAD ticket includes one drink. Capacity is capped at 60 so the room still feels human. No stage, no speaker list, no forced intros. The bar will have alcoholic and non-alcoholic options. Come Work From FQ First Your ticket includes access to the FriendsQuarters members lounge earlier the same day. Bring your laptop, get the last thing of the week done from FQ, and stay right where you are when the bar opens at 4:00. Check in at the front desk when you arrive. Kris will often be working from the lounge that afternoon, so come find him, or just claim a couch and get your own thing done until the room fills up. This Month Last one of the year. Half the room will have already done three holiday parties this week, and this is the one where nobody makes you do a toast or wear a name tag. Come tell us what you actually shipped in 2026 and what you are not going to repeat in 2027. Details When: Friday, December 18, 2026, 4:00-7:00 PM Where: FriendsQuarters (FQ) 116 Lounge, 200-116 West Hastings St, Vancouver Tickets: $10 CAD. Includes one drink. Registration required. Capacity: 60. Cadence: 3rd Friday at FQ. Hosted by Kris Krüg and the BC + AI community with Dean Lariviere and FriendsQuarters. The Hosts FriendsQuarters is a media, event and co-working space on the edge of Gastown, with exposed brick, a bar, private patio, and a podcast studio, run by Dean and crew on the principle that friends make work. It is BC + AI's second home in downtown Vancouver. BC + AI, led by Kris Krüg, is a grassroots network of educators, technologists, artists, and community builders shaping a uniquely BC approach to AI, rooted in accessibility, community, and ethical design. Questions or want to get involved? kk@bc-ai.ca About BC + AI Part solarpunk R&D lab, part community potluck. BC + AI brings curious humans together to make things, ask hard questions, and have a say in where this technology takes us. We’re a member-driven nonprofit building public-interest infrastructure for AI in British Columbia. A commons where meetups turn into working groups, prototypes turn into shared tools, and community values turn into governance. Vancouver AI was the first room. The work keeps growing through the people who show up and give a damn. Multi-modal, multi-cultural, future-facing, and radically local. Meet BC + AI Plug into the bigger organism Bring the half-working thing. Somebody here might know what to do with it. Membership helps keep this whole strange, useful organism alive. Bring a stuck project to Office Hours, find collaborators through the directory, or help start the working group you wish existed. Keep making things together between meetups. Your dues help sustain the rooms, the connections, and the knowledge we put back into public. Join BC + AI. Help build what happens next. Other upcoming BC + AI events Nov 11, 2026 18:00 (America/Vancouver): FV + AI November: Fraser Valley AI Community Meetup Nov 12, 2026 18:30 (America/Vancouver): AI Film Club with Kevin Friel | Nov 12 Nov 19, 2026 18:30 (America/Vancouver): ED + AI #15: What It Gave Back, What It Took See the full BC + AI calendar More ways to take part Find your community: Regional chapters and focused rooms across British Columbia. Learn through a program: Responsible AI, animation, creative workflows, and local AI. Explore what we make public: Guides, tools, reading trails, and shared knowledge. Watch the recordings: Talks, demos, panels, and community work. Stay in the loop Get field notes, upcoming gatherings, program calls, and useful work from across the ecosystem. Subscribe to the BC + AI newsletter",
